# Marketplace Credentials — Never to Frontend

## Rule

**Marketplace credentials must NEVER be sent to the frontend under any circumstances.** Ozon (clientId, apiKey) and Wildberries (apiKey) are secrets used only server-side for API calls.

## What Frontend May Receive

At most:
- `marketAccountId` (or `id`) — to trigger operations (e.g. POST sync/import with `marketAccountId`)
- `marketplace` — OZON | WILDBERRIES
- `name`, `isActive`, `createdAt` — non-sensitive metadata

## What Must NEVER Be in API Responses

- `credentialsEncrypted`
- `credentialsHash`
- `credentialsVersion`
- Any decrypted fields: `clientId`, `apiKey`, tokens

## Implementation

- `MarketAccount` list/detail endpoints: use Prisma `select` to exclude credential fields
- DTOs and Swagger schemas: never expose credential types
- If adding new endpoints returning MarketAccount data — verify `select` or transform omits credentials

## Where Credentials Are Used

- Backend only: `CredentialsCryptoService.decrypt()` in services/workers
- Workers: import processor, sync processors — decrypt, pass to Ozon/WB HTTP client
